WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
Kaze ni kami ga nabiku

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
My hair flows in the wind.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
Kokoro ni hirogaru aozora no deai

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
An encounter in the blue skies of our hearts...

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Though we are apart,

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Tooku hanaretetemo

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
I'm always thinking about you,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
Kanjiru koto wa itsumo kimi dakara

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
so let's promise to meet again

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
Itsu no hi ka mune wo hatte

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
one day, with our heads held high.

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
Au koto wo yakusoku shiyou

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
We'll be together, like a dream

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
Zutto futari owari no nai

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
with no end.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
Yume wo egaku you ni

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
I want

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
Kimi ni

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
to tell you this someday.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
Kono omoi itsu no hi ka tsutaetai

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
I'm right here next to you

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
Sabishisa wo shiawase ni kaeru tame

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
to turn your loneliness into joy.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
Soba ni iru yo kokoro wa

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
I can feel your heart so close to mine.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
Konna ni chikaku ni kanjiru

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:38.430
Because of Onodera's scheming, all the costumes and set used by Maya's troupe have been destroyed,

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:43.540
and the rest of the troupe are now trapped in the mountains.

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:45.560
As the hour of performance draws near,

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:49.490
Maya decides to play all the parts herself.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:56.080
Episode 12 - Alone on Stage

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:09.460
I'm putting on her mask...

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:16.420
Gina's mask.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:40.960
I'll look after the house until tomorrow.

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:45.030
Yes, I'll be careful of strangers!

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:48.420
Goodbye, Dad!

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:51.830
She skipped the father's lines.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:53.250
But we still understand what's going on.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:56.600
Yeah, we can understand the scene just through her lines!

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:13.860
Yes, who is it?

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:17.210
You say you're a traveler?

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.890
What can I do for you?

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:20.860
You're being chased?

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.250
And you want me to watch this jar for you?

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.170
I can't do that!

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:30.960
But, hold on a sec... I'm not that kind of girl!

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.140
If you tell me not to look in it, I won't!

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:34.850
No, I told you, I can't!

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:36.980
Hey, wait... Mister!

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.450
I guess that means I'm looking after it...

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:50.360
Are they hiding the rest of the troupe on purpose?

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:53.700
Or is this a new technique?

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:11.480
You're one of the King's knights and you're searching for a man with a blue jar?

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:17.800
He's hidden the royal seal between our nation and our neighbors in that jar?

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:19.800
It can't be...

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:26.950
Ow! Let go of me!

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:31.150
I don't know any men with blue jars!

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:32.480
It's the truth!

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:39.270
All right... I won't tell anyone!

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:42.480
So, please... put that sword away!

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:55.000
What's going on? Why aren't they showing any of the other characters?

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:57.840
A little while ago, someone told me...

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:02.720
that the other members of that girl's troupe have gone missing.

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:04.460
We're really sorry.

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:09.070
The car broke down and I couldn't get a signal to call up here in the mountains.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:13.230
What? Is that true?!

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:17.210
Maya's doing the play by herself?

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:20.870
I'm not quite sure... but there might be a jewel hidden in that jar.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:26.490
Gosh! There are four sets of people looking for it now.

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:29.900
What on earth could be inside?

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:41.040
This is...

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:46.230
Squeak, squeak!

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:50.940
Mice! Take that! Come back here!

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:57.920
She's doing a sterling job.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:02.980
It's important to have some comic relief in a suspense play.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:10.990
I really should just throw this thing away.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:14.450
No, I can't do that!

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:16.960
I must keep it safe.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.710
We've reached the intermission.

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:29.230
It's certainly an interesting performance, but there haven't been any other actors so far.

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:31.120
What's the meaning of this?

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:33.190
What did you think, ma'am?

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:35.080
It's going pretty well, isn't it?

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:39.010
Now I just have to make it through the second half.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.130
Maya...

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:45.280
I underestimated that girl.

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:47.310
I don't believe it.

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:49.630
She's actually going to try to finish the play all by herself.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:51.440
Well, she's not going to be able to keep this up!

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:54.640
It's all going to fall apart from here on out.

00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:01.640
Ms. Tsukikage... it looks like she might be able to keep this up...

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:03.130
until the others get back.

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:05.640
No, the others won't make it in time.

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.270
Then...

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:09.210
The second half is going to be a problem...

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:15.660
Three knights, an official, a snake charmer, a queen and her servant,

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:19.850
her father, the traveler... all those roles...

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:25.390
Yes, all the other thirteen characters come into the house at the same time!

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:32.440
We can't let it end until that girl steps off the stage!

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:33.400
Maya!

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:41.410
There! I did it!

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:46.230
Now no one can get in, no matter who happens to knock on my door!

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:52.150
Done.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:56.800
I've filled the whole house with blue jars.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:59.230
If you want to hide a stone, you put it in a pile of pebbles...

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:03.130
So, if you want to hide a blue jar, this is how you do it!

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:13.580
Oh, the knights have returned!

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:17.050
Someone told you the blue jar was here?

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:21.400
No, I can't open the door, because I promised my father I wouldn't!

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:27.350
Wait! Stop banging on the door! Just tell me which jar you're looking for?

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:30.550
This jar has pickles in it...

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:34.170
This one has sour wine...

00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:39.210
She's going to make it through the whole scene without letting the knights inside!

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:42.080
What's wrong? You don't want to keep looking?

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:45.030
Oh, it's the soldiers from the castle!

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:58.190
Thank you for getting those knights to go away!

00:08:58.190 --> 00:09:01.000
You were wonderful, kind sirs!

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:06.790
Did you find what you were looking for?

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:08.420
Here, have some water!

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:11.060
That's fantastic!

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:18.010
The knights have been arrested and it seems the blue jar with the royal seal is safe.

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:23.000
The love potion the queen was searching for turned out to be a fake as well...

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:28.010
and we found the blue jar containing the snake charmer's poisonous snake.

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:31.600
Now all that remains is the jewel that was stolen by the killer-thief.

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:36.600
Maybe that was the jar I took from the stranger!

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:03.650
Oh, the window...

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:09.850
That was impressive!

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:12.320
Yeah, to be able to convey so much tension just by extending her hand!

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:14.010
Impressive!

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:18.730
Who's there?

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:21.340
A servant of the official?

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:23.040
You've found him, you say?

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:26.280
The man who assassinated someone to steal a jewel?

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:30.490
Thank you so much for coming to tell me!

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:38.630
Now I can take this barricade down!

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:43.080
Is this really the same girl who stood crying in the rain,

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:45.840
because she was so worried about the play?

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:04.820
The door was open...

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:15.410
The jars are all opened!

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:17.790
But I don't remember opening them...

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:24.060
We've reached the climax...

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:27.070
If she can pull this off, then...

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:38.770
Who's there?

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:40.700
Is there someone there?!

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:08.310
Who... Who are you?!

00:12:11.020 --> 00:12:12.550
You're doing great, Maya...

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:15.550
Your reactions are perfect!

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:22.700
That hurts! Let go of me!

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:30.200
Now!

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:49.300
Aren't you the man who came to tell me about the arrest?

00:12:50.070 --> 00:12:53.780
So, you're the thief!

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:58.750
Help! Murderer! Murderer!

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:02.370
Help! Someone please help me!

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:09.390
You... please arrest that thief... he's in here!

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:19.300
Thank you for catching the thief.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:24.430
Wait, you're trying to tell me that the jar contained stewed apples all along?!

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:26.640
And that's why you had a wild dog chasing you...

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:30.540
You were planning on giving the jar to your mother out in the country,

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:34.920
which is why you told me it was important...

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:40.460
Goodbye!

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:42.630
I hope you get home safely!

00:13:44.770 --> 00:13:49.330
Wow, it's morning already! So much has happened!

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:51.970
I can't believe all that happened in a single day!

00:14:00.260 --> 00:14:01.810
Dad!

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:06.820
Welcome home! You must be exhausted.

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:08.430
I'll fix you up something to eat right away...

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:11.360
I've made a scrumptious soup for you...

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:24.890
Why is everyone so quiet?

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:40.270
Go, Maya...

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:43.030
It's a curtain call.

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:44.380
A curtain call?

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:46.900
For me?!

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:51.010
That girl...

00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:52.680
...is very strange!

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:54.770
And yet, she has such a strong stage presence.

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:56.580
What are you doing, Maya?

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:58.390
You're meant to stand in the middle of the stage!

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:00.000
Oh... Oh!

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:06.650
I... I just wanted to say thank you very much for your...

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:12.370
You don't have to say anything! Just come back over here!

00:15:16.170 --> 00:15:18.150
<i>Thank you</i>!

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:24.130
We shouldn't have let her take the curtain call.

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:33.810
Watching her sleep, she looks just like any other girl.

00:15:34.420 --> 00:15:37.820
What is she keeping inside of herself?

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:49.080
The judges have yet to decide on the results, but we will now announce...

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:53.570
the audience's top three.

00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:58.460
Starting with third place, we have the Ondine Troupe who performed <i>The Ashen Castle</i>.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:02.970
Third place?

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:08.690
In second, we have Hokkaido's representative, the Ikkakujuu Troupe, with <i>Fate</i>.

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:15.840
And first place goes to Tokyo's Tsukikage Acting Troupe and their rendition of...

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:18.360
<i>Gina and the Five Blue Jars.</i>

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:20.350
Maya, you did it!

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:27.400
That girl... Last year, she was peeking in on our rehearsals...

00:16:27.740 --> 00:16:30.720
That girl... She didn't even know what pantomime was...

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:33.390
What's wrong?

00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:37.460
There's a possibility we may be disqualified from the competition.

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:40.640
And now that the judges have finalized their decision...

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:42.390
One moment, please!

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:47.770
I would like the judges of the Japanese National Acting Competition...

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:52.370
to consider revising their judgment regarding one of the groups!

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:53.760
Mr. Onodera?

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:58.970
The Tsukikage Acting Troupe's <i>Gina and the Five Blue Jars</i>...

00:16:58.970 --> 00:17:03.760
was too far removed from what we call "traditional acting" or if you rather, the spirit of the theater!

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:09.570
There are supposed to be fourteen characters in the play, and yet the whole play...

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:11.960
was performed by a single person!

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:15.910
That's because the other actors of the troupe weren't present!

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:17.090
Hold on a minute!

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:18.630
We've got a very good reason for that!

00:17:18.630 --> 00:17:22.010
The reason behind it is beyond the point!

00:17:23.550 --> 00:17:28.360
And then, the actor on stage took too many liberties with the script,

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:30.690
cutting out lines and ad-libbing new ones when it suited her!

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:35.830
This is an insult to proper acting!

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:45.030
If you win this competition, Aoyagi Productions will have no choice...

00:17:45.030 --> 00:17:49.660
but to withdraw their support from your troupe.

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:52.000
Without their assistance...

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:56.640
you will have to remove yourself from the classrooms...

00:17:56.660 --> 00:18:01.620
Japanese National Acting Competition

00:17:57.350 --> 00:18:01.620
We thank you for your patience and would like to announce the revised results.

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:04.890
Starting with third place, we have the representatives from Yamaguchi,

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:07.510
the Ohagi Troupe, with their version of <i>Fukurokouji</i>.

00:18:08.110 --> 00:18:11.130
But they were only fifth in the audience vote...

00:18:11.130 --> 00:18:16.510
Second place goes to Hokkaido's Ikkakujuu, with <i>Fate</i>.

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:18.550
<i>All right</i>!

00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:22.560
And the winner of the competition is Tokyo's representative...

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:31.990
the Ondine Troupe, with <i>The Ashen Castle</i>.

00:18:32.280 --> 00:18:34.390
Yeah!

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:47.100
As for the Tsukikage Acting Troupe's <i>Gina and the Five Blue Jars,</i>

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:52.000
it was determined that their performance broke too many conventional rules...

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:54.140
and has thus been removed from consideration.

00:18:58.890 --> 00:19:02.450
Maya, stop beating yourself up about it!

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:07.990
What's wrong, O tragic heroine?

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:12.670
Gina, who fought off a thief in the pitch black all by herself, starts crying...

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:15.230
as soon as she steps off stage?

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:17.680
I refuse to use your handkerchief!

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:21.590
Oh look, it's that actress who doesn't care about the spirit of acting.

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:22.980
Cut it out!

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:25.600
Shut it, will you?

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:27.400
Ayumi...

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:32.620
I look forward to the next time we meet on stage.

00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:37.130
And next time, I <i>won't</i> lose!

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:41.410
Ayumi, why did you say something like that?

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:43.140
You didn't lose to her!

00:19:43.730 --> 00:19:49.150
I don't feel like I lost to her in skill, no.

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:54.130
But look at that... she draws a crowd.

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:58.640
And the people - the audience - <i>they</i> chose her.

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:02.390
Our whole troupe lost to her even though she was all by herself.

00:20:02.390 --> 00:20:05.350
Even when our performance is long forgotten,

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:09.870
her feat of carrying a whole play by herself for an hour and forty-five minutes...

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:13.520
That will go down in legend.

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:15.700
The Tsukikage Acting Troupe

00:20:14.280 --> 00:20:17.780
Even if the official results state that she was defeated.

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:25.290
Ma'am...

00:20:26.920 --> 00:20:28.780
Ma'am! I want to apologize.

00:20:28.780 --> 00:20:30.250
It's my fault that...

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:31.770
No.

00:20:31.770 --> 00:20:35.010
Maya, you did exceedingly well.

00:20:35.270 --> 00:20:40.010
But now... the Tsukikage Acting Troupe will disband...

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:44.470
Let's just accept it.

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:52.140
But, ma'am! I don't want to stop acting!

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:56.010
I'll work part-time so that I won't be a burden... Please! I'll do anything...

00:20:56.010 --> 00:20:58.950
Please! Let me stay with you!

00:20:58.950 --> 00:21:01.930
Maya... it's not just about you, you know!

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:05.400
We want to stay with you too!

00:21:05.400 --> 00:21:08.540
If we all work together, we can achieve great things!

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:12.570
We want to keep acting with you.

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:14.260
All right.

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:16.300
Oh thank you, ma'am!

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:32.870
The acting school that Chigusa Tsukikage poured her soul into...

00:21:32.870 --> 00:21:35.220
has finally been forced to close its doors.

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:40.370
What's in store for Maya and the other students...

00:21:40.370 --> 00:21:43.670
who have agreed to carry on with her?

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:48.610
This is the beginning of a new test.

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.930
Gomennette iwaretara

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.930
When you say "I'm sorry,"

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:10.670
Anata wo semerarenai yo

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:10.670
I can't blame you.

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:21.510
Sonna watashi wo kitto shitterundeshou

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:21.510
I'm sure you know that's how I am.

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:25.810
Nee zurui yo

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:25.810
That's not fair.

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:33.620
Yasashisa ni damasaretatte

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:33.620
Even if I'm being fooled by kindness,

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:44.210
Anata nara isso iito shinjita

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:44.210
I believed that with you, it might be worth it.

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:53.690
Sayonara wa doushite itoshiindarou

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:53.690
Why are goodbyes so precious,

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.250
Hanareteyuku noni

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.250
even though they mean we're separating?

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:07.640
Ushinatta ondo wo oboeteruyo

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:07.640
I remember how it got colder.

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.500
Yurushitai dakara anata

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.500
I want to forgive you, so please don't go.

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:21.410
Ikanaide douka ikanaide

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:21.410
Whatever you do... just don't go.

00:23:22.070 --> 00:23:26.480
Maya... even though you've done such a spectacular job by yourself on stage,

00:23:26.480 --> 00:23:29.700
the Tsukikage Acting Troupe has been forced to disband.

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:32.850
I hear that all the members...

00:23:32.850 --> 00:23:36.420
who decided to stay are supporting their acting career with part-time jobs.

00:23:36.620 --> 00:23:40.350
But I'm sure you want to devote all your time to rehearsing,

00:23:40.840 --> 00:23:43.520
so why don't you come and join our troupe, Maya?

00:23:43.950 --> 00:23:46.740
Director Onodera says he'd wave the tuition fees for you.

00:23:46.910 --> 00:23:51.200
Episode 13 - Tomorrow's Grass

00:23:47.100 --> 00:23:50.010
I want to get up on stage with you, Maya!
